{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "aws-lambda-telemetry-analytics-v1",
  "title": "Serverless workload telemetry into searchable operations analytics",
  "subtitle": "A function runtime emits logs and metrics through an extension/collector path to a search-oriented analytics store. Synthetic Azure reference; no deployment is implied.",
  "description": "### Problem\nOperators need searchable, timely telemetry from event-driven application functions, with useful views for troubleshooting and service health.\n\n### Flow and Azure mapping\nFunctions emit structured logs and metrics to Azure Monitor through supported instrumentation or a collector. Diagnostic settings and data collection rules route selected records to Log Analytics or an Azure Data Explorer workspace. Workbooks or dashboards let operators correlate requests, dependencies, and failures. A separate export path can deliver governed records to an external observability platform if required.\n\n### Trade-offs and assumptions\nThe AWS source uses a Lambda Telemetry API extension to send telemetry directly to OpenSearch, bypassing its default log intermediary. Azure Monitor is the natural Azure-native baseline, but not a direct OpenSearch substitute; high-cardinality data, retention, sampling, ingestion volume, and query costs need sizing. Avoid routing every verbose trace or sensitive payload into long-retention logs. The graph is an observability pattern, not an application architecture.\n\nSource: [AWS Prescriptive Guidance](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/patterns/send-telemetry-data-from-lambda-to-opensearch-for-analytics-visualization.html).\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- Origin provider: AWS\n- Target: Azure conceptual adaptation\n- Primary source: [Send telemetry data from AWS Lambda to OpenSearch for real-time analytics and visualization](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/prescriptive-guidance/latest/patterns/send-telemetry-data-from-lambda-to-opensearch-for-analytics-visualization.html)\n- Reviewed: 2026-11-06\n\n## Catalog status\n\nThis is an original, editable Azure conceptual adaptation. It is synthetic reference material, not a deployed system, certified vendor architecture, or automatic deployment plan.\n\n## Mapping caveats\n\n- Azure Monitor and OpenSearch have different data models, retention, query languages, and cost dimensions.",
